From 65f188f6250cf43a8a0f6295529e5e74e2209715 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:20:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): don't refuse a runs_on card over this machine's
 profiles [daveey]

A card whose runs_on rules this machine out (e.g. placement=hub rewritten to
runs_on=[machine:hub]) runs with the landing machine's profile of that name.
create_task still ran validate_assignment, the skills check, the managed model
registry check and provider binding against THIS machine's profiles, so
kanban_create(assignee=bb-tuner, placement=hub) from the MacBook was refused
with 'Profile bb-tuner does not exist' although bb-tuner exists on the hub.

- runs_elsewhere(conn, runs_on): machine:<other> label, or labels the registry
  says this machine lacks (registry unreachable or not a primary: local checks).
- create_task's assignee checks move to kanban_db_creation.validate_create_assignment.
  For a remote card it validates only the requires shape; check_create still
  refuses when every landing machine publishes tools that lack a need, and
  claim_refusal re-checks tools at pickup.
- Pinned skills defer to the landing worker (missing_pin_note), never a pickup
  gate, so a remote card is not stranded; the model registry defers to the
  landing dispatcher (route_model_mismatch). A vendor/provider family mismatch
  is still refused.
- A remote card's concrete provider-less pin is refused with the providers to
  pass (require_remote_pin_provider): this machine's credentials can't bind it
  and the landing dispatcher would only late-bind it at spawn.
- Cards that can run here keep every local check.
